.TH GWAY-LCD-SOUND 1 "2026-10-18" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gway-lcd-sound \- release-owned LCD and sound helper dispatcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gway-lcd-sound
.B monitor eth0
.RI [ monitor-options ]
.br
.B gway-lcd-sound
.B hotplug
.I event
.br
.B gway-lcd-sound
.B mute toggle
.RI [ --status ]
.br
.B gway-lcd-sound
.B notify
.RI [ notify-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gway-lcd-sound
dispatches user-level LCD and sound helper commands from the active LCD Sound
release. It replaces its process with the selected helper, so monitor and
hotplug signal and exit behavior are preserved.
.PP
The installer keeps the command at
.I ~/.local/bin/gway-lcd-sound
and installs this manual page at
.IR ~/.local/share/man/man1/gway-lcd-sound.1 .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B monitor eth0
Runs the Ethernet LCD monitor. Remaining options are passed to the monitor,
including
.BR --interval ,
.BR --once ,
and
.BR --no-scan .
.TP
.B hotplug event
Passes the event to the release-owned hotplug helper. The helper uses
.I GWAY_SOUND_BIN
when set, otherwise
.IR /usr/local/bin/sound .
.TP
.B mute toggle
Toggles GPIO sound mute state. With
.B --status
it reports the state without changing it.
.TP
.B notify
Passes notification options through to the release-owned notifier. It accepts
.BR --channel ,
.BR --subject ,
.BR --body-file ,
.BR --body ,
.BR --attach ,
and
.BR --dry-run .
.SH COMPATIBILITY
The former standalone helper files are not overwritten or deleted by the
release installer. Root-owned systemd and udev configuration must be migrated
separately under field-change approval. Retire a standalone helper only after
its consumers have been audited and the backup procedure in the repository
operations documentation has completed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/gway-lcd-sound/current
The active release selected by the installer.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/gway-lcd-sound
Stable link to the dispatcher in the active release.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lcd-lockfile-runner (1),
.BR sound (1)
